  "sdkFixCommit": "4e4d825e",
  "fix": [
    "Start main-thread Yao module initialization in shared NEAR passkey registration warmup, including the NEAR-only path.",
    "Start near-signer module initialization when the NEAR custody ceremony begins, overlapping the Router request.",
    "Share one retryable main-thread module initialization promise, so overlapping preload and activation cannot replace the live WASM instance.",
    "Keep capability establishment, session validation, persistence, and secret operations in their original authorized order."
  ],
  "comparisonLimits": [
    "The historical 0.13 baseline served iframe assets locally. It hid these network transfers.",
    "The three affected registration/client/worker source files did not change between the published 0.13 and 0.15.4 commits. The measured asset cost is not evidence of a newly introduced 0.15 SDK computation cost.",
    "The earlier pooled 588 ms local SDK gap vanished in tighter interleaving: 1768 ms vs 1777.5 ms medians. Route composition differed in the pooled comparison.",
    "This fix does not explain the separate NRT production warmup with 5021 ms respond and 6769 ms post-passkey duration. A/B elapsed protocol time greatly exceeded own invocation CPU; the precise backend wait remains unresolved.",
    "Production has not received this SDK change. No production latency improvement is claimed."
  ],
  "otherInvestigations": {
    "network": "Fixed-address probes reproduced PDX TCP connect around 131 ms followed by NRT around 11 ms at the same address. This establishes transport variation before Wallet execution.",
    "storage": "Staging A/B storage-sync observer was removed and all original worker versions restored. No multi-second acknowledgement was captured. Route changes confounded aggregate before/observed/after latency, so no storage speedup is claimed."
  },
